nodecode-tavily is a rewrite of tavily-ai's tavily-ai/tavily-hermes-plugin:

  https://github.com/tavily-ai/tavily-hermes-plugin
  commit ac556341056dc903988f63d627d595e468f1cfa9
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Tavily AI (LICENSE)

The plugin was a portable manifest (plugin.json) and one mcp.json entry that
pointed Hermes at Tavily's hosted MCP server, https://mcp.tavily.com/mcp/,
authenticated with a bearer TAVILY_API_KEY or a Hermes-managed OAuth sign-in,
plus six skills adapted from tavily-ai/skills. The server advertised five
tools, and every one of them was one Tavily REST endpoint: search, extract,
map, crawl and research. This rewrite keeps the five tool names, their
argument names and the same endpoints, and posts to them itself through
nlk:http, so no MCP transport, no Node and no local server are needed. The
skills' guidance -- search to discover, extract what matters, bound a crawl,
one report per question, cite the urls, stop on a credit or rate limit -- is
the cell's manual topic, (help :tavily), and each tool's argument list is its
declared schema. What was left out: the OAuth sign-in (a cell's section is
one key, and Hermes owned the token store, so an API key is the way in here),
the MCP timeout override, and the remote tools' schema discovery, which the
declarations replace. Nothing of the original is vendored.
